    {
      "source": "candidate retainedNativeCustody.ts:318-321; CapturedHostClient.ts:510-515",
      "finding": "The same entry deadline is shortened with Math.min(existing,performance.now()+20). Only then is the one-shot flag set and original admitted resolver called. The original Map.set result is returned; only after that return does Main install its original timer from the capped deadline and call its original pump."
    },
    {
      "source": "candidate retainedNativeCustody.ts:328-360; capturedHostClient.test.ts:354-371",
      "finding": "The original child stdin write still occurs once. Only its original completion callback is held after actual write completion; blocked and queued races remain mandatory. The gate does not forge a native frame, insert a synthetic entry, complete a missing admission or replace the real child stream."
